title: Opening a file with another program
tags: GUI
kind: guide
aliases: open-with file:open-with xdg-open external-program
summary: Hand the selected file or folder to another program — the desktop's default, an image editor, a player — from any panel.

What the GUI cannot show itself goes to another program. Select the file or folder
in any panel carrying the selection — the list, the detail, `file`, the file manager,
`recent`, `treeref` — and run `file:open-with` (<<key "file:open-with" "g w">>), or
choose ''Open with…'' in the right-click menu of a file row, which selects that row
first.

The command input asks for the program ([[Interactive command arguments]]), completing over the `open-with` list of
[[GUI configuration]] — by default `["xdg-open"]`, the desktop's own choice for that
kind of file:

```
open-with = ["xdg-open", "mpv", "gimp", "gimp -n"]
```

That list is a set of suggestions, not a limit: any command line may be typed, and it
is run as typed — flags included (`gimp -n`, `env FOO=1 mpv`) — with the selected
paths quoted and appended.

It runs like a `!` command: the program's output goes to the [[message panel]], and the
task bar shows it while it runs ([[Status bar and task bar]]). Unlike a `!` command,
it does not switch the focused slot to the [[message panel]] — opening a viewer should
leave the screen as it was.

With nothing selected, it says ''no file or folder is selected'' and does nothing.
